1	# Redblue
     2	
     3	[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
     4	[![Rust](https://img.shields.io/badge/Rust-1.70+-dea584.svg?logo=rust)](https://www.rust-lang.org)
     5	
     6	**Redblue** is a programming language designed to be as readable as plain English. Write code that reads like natural sentences while maintaining the power of modern programming languages.
     7	
     8	```redblue
     9	// Hello World
    10	say "Hello, World!"
    11	
    12	// Functions - readable and clear
    13	to greet(name)
    14	    say "Hello, {name}!"
    15	end
    16	
    17	// Control flow - no cryptic symbols
    18	if count is greater than 10
    19	    say "Large count!"
    20	else
    21	    say "Small count!"
    22	end
    23	
    24	// Objects - simple and intuitive
    25	object Person
    26	    has name
    27	    has age
    28	    
    29	    to introduce()
    30	        say "I'm {this.name}"
    31	    end
    32	end
    33	```
    34	
    35	## Why Redblue?
    36	
    37	| Feature | Redblue | Python | JavaScript |
    38	|---------|---------|--------|------------|
    39	| Keywords | 32 | 35 | 50+ |
    40	| Readability | ★★★★★ | ★★★★☆ | ★★★☆☆ |
    41	| Plain English syntax | Yes | No | No |
    42	
    43	- **32 keywords** vs Python's 35 and JavaScript's 50+
    44	- Code reads like instructions you'd give a person
    45	- No cryptic symbols: `end` not `}`, `each` not `for...of`
    46	
