   313	## 5. Expressions
   314	
   315	### 5.1 Primary Expressions
   316	
   317	```
   318	primary          = identifier
   319	                 | literal
   320	                 | '(' expression ')'
   321	                 | list_literal
   322	                 | record_literal
   323	                 | function_literal
   324	                 | object_literal
   325	```
   326	
   327	### 5.2 Postfix Expressions
   328	
   329	```
   330	postfix          = primary
   331	                 | postfix '.' identifier              // property access
   332	                 | postfix '(' [ argument { ',' argument } ] ')'  // function call
   333	                 | postfix '[' expression ']'         // indexing
   334	                 | postfix 'of' expression            // generic type
   335	```
   336	
   337	### 5.3 Prefix Expressions
   338	
   339	```
   340	prefix           = postfix
   341	                 | 'not' prefix
   342	                 | '-' prefix                          // negation
   343	```
   344	
   345	### 5.4 Multiplicative Expressions
   346	
   347	```
   348	multiplicative   = prefix
   349	                 | multiplicative '*' prefix           // multiply
   350	                 | multiplicative '/' prefix           // divide
   351	                 | multiplicative 'mod' prefix         // modulo
   352	```
   353	
   354	### 5.5 Additive Expressions
   355	
   356	```
   357	additive         = multiplicative
   358	                 | additive '+' multiplicative         // add
   359	                 | additive '-' multiplicative        // subtract
   360	```
   361	
   362	### 5.6 Comparison Expressions
   363	
   364	```
   365	comparison       = additive
   366	                 | comparison 'is equal to' additive   // ==
   367	                 | comparison 'is not' additive       // !=
   368	                 | comparison 'is less than' additive // <
   369	                 | comparison 'is greater than' additive // >
   370	                 | comparison 'is less than or equal to' additive // <=
   371	                 | comparison 'is greater than or equal to' additive // >=
   372	                 | comparison 'in' additive           // in (contains)
   373	```
   374	
   375	### 5.7 Logical AND Expressions
   376	
   377	```
   378	logical_and      = comparison
   379	                 | logical_and 'and' comparison       // &&
   380	```
   381	
   382	### 5.8 Logical OR Expressions
   383	
   384	```
   385	logical_or       = logical_and
   386	                 | logical_or 'or' logical_and       // ||
   387	```
   388	
   389	### 5.9 Conditional Expression (Ternary)
   390	
   391	```
   392	conditional      = logical_or
   393	                 | logical_or '?' expression ':' conditional
   394	                 | logical_or 'if' expression 'else' conditional
   395	```
   396	
   397	### 5.10 Assignment Expression
   398	
   399	```
   400	assignment_expr  = conditional
   401	                 | identifier 'to' assignment_expr    // assignment
   402	```
   403	
   404	### 5.11 Expression (Final)
   405	
   406	```
   407	expression       = assignment_expr
   408	                 | 'might fail' expression            // error propagation
   409	```
   410	
   411	---
   412	
   413	## 6. Function Literals
   414	
   415	```
   416	function_literal = 'to' [ '(' [ parameter { ',' parameter } ] ')' ]
   417	                    { statement }
   418	                    'end'
   419	```
   420	
   421	---
   422	
   423	## 7. Object Literals
   424	
   425	```
   426	object_literal   = 'new' identifier '(' [ argument { ',' argument } ] ')'
   427	```
   428	
   429	---
   430	
   431	## 8. Precedence Table (Lowest to Highest)
   432	
   433	| Precedence | Operator(s) | Associativity |
   434	|------------|-------------|---------------|
   435	| 1 | `or` | Left |
   436	| 2 | `and` | Left |
   437	| 3 | `is`, `is not`, `in` | Left |
   438	| 4 | `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` | Left |
   439	| 5 | `+`, `-` | Left |
   440	| 6 | `*`, `/`, `mod` | Left |
   441	| 7 | `not`, unary `-` | Right |
   442	| 8 | `of` | Left |
   443	| 9 | property access, call, index | Left |
   444	
   445	---
   446	
   447	## 9. Syntax Examples
   448	
   449	### Hello World
   450	```redblue
   451	say "Hello, World!"
   452	```
   453	
   454	### Variable Declaration
   455	```redblue
   456	set name to "Alice"
   457	set age to 30
   458	set items to [1, 2, 3]
   459	```
   460	
   461	### If Statement
   462	```redblue
   463	if age is greater than 18
   464	    say "You can vote"
   465	else
   466	    say "Too young to vote"
   467	end
   468	```
   469	
   470	### For Loop
   471	```redblue
   472	for each i from 1 to 10
   473	    say i
   474	end
   475	```
   476	
   477	### Function
   478	```redblue
   479	to add(a, b)
   480	    give back a + b
   481	end
   482	
   483	set result to add(1, 2)
   484	```
   485	
   486	### Object
   487	```redblue
   488	object Person
   489	    has name
   490	    has age
   491	    
   492	    to introduce()
   493	        say "I'm {this.name}"
   494	    end
   495	end
   496	
   497	set person to new Person
   498	set name of person to "Bob"
   499	person.introduce()
   500	```
   501	
   502	### Try/Catch
   503	```redblue
   504	try
   505	    set data to might fail files.read("config.txt")
   506	    say data
   507	catch error
   508	    say "Failed to read file: {error message}"
   509	end
   510	```
   511	
   512	---
   513	
   514	## 10. Grammar Files
   515	
   516	This grammar will be implemented using:
   517	- **Lexer**: Custom tokenizer or Logos/Lark
   518	- **Parser**: Recursive descent or Lark parser generator
   519	- **Validator**: Semantic analysis after parsing
   520	
   521	---
   522	
   523	*Grammar v1.0 - March 2026*
